Tons of customization and tuning, fun gameplay, lots to do and mess around with. My two gripes in the short time I've played as are follows;
1. Cornering. Drifting feels great, but that's where the fun cornering stops. Track oriented cars hook so much on corners but for some reason, your character is unable to turn his steering wheel more than halfway. This means you get stuck in this gradual, slow turn that isn't accurate at all of track built cars. I'm sorry, but a lambo can take a 90 degree turn over 25mph and stay on the throttle. It just feels sluggish.
